#====================================================================
# E2155 - Clear Conan's default include directory for headerless libraries
#====================================================================

id:                     E498
trigger_tool:           conan|cmake
phase:                  package|consumer-configuration|linking
error_signature:        imported target.*non-existent.*include|INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES.*does not exist|CMakeDeps.*include.*does not exist

severity:               3
category:               cmake, conan, packaging, api, headerless-library
match_keywords:         Conan 2, CMakeDeps, cpp_info.includedirs, include directory, imported target, headerless library, package metadata
title:                  Clear Conan's default include directory for a headerless library

root_cause:             Conan defaults cpp_info.includedirs to include even when a package intentionally installs no public headers, so CMakeDeps exports a usage requirement for a directory that does not exist.
affected_scope:         Conan library recipes that install linkable libraries and metadata but intentionally expose no public headers.
verification_cmd:       Configure, compile, link, and run a consumer that uses only the generated imported target; require no hard-coded include or library paths and no nonexistent include-directory diagnostic.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           explicit-empty-public-include-contract
rec_description:        Set self.cpp_info.includedirs to an empty list while preserving the real public libraries, transitive requirements, target names, and system libraries.
rec_command:            Add self.cpp_info.includedirs = [] in package_info() and rerun a CMakeDeps imported-target consumer.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               manual-conan-package-info

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      install-missing-public-headers
fallback_description:   If the library actually has a public header API, install the missing headers and keep a real include directory instead of clearing metadata.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       target_include_directories.*package_folder|include_directories.*\.conan|CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH.*include
forbid_1_reason:        Consumer-side hard-coded paths bypass the generated package contract.
forbid_1_consequence:   The test can pass while downstream CMakeDeps consumers still fail.

forbid_2_pattern:       includedirs.*\[\].*public headers installed
forbid_2_reason:        Clearing include metadata is valid only for a genuinely headerless public contract.
forbid_2_consequence:   Real header consumers lose their required usage path.

principles:             P012
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E221]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E2155-draft-2301.md
last_updated:           2026-08-19
source_event:           ScaLAPACK 2.2.3 r8 failed after packaging on a nonexistent include path; r10 passed the real generated-target consumer.

authors: 2301_80739235 <2047361658@qq.com>
source_pr: !5839
source_commit:

metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     1.0
